<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · South America</p><h1 class="st-title">Granadine Confederation</h1><p class="st-meta">1858 CE – 1863 CE · capital Bogotá</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Colombia's experiment with a confederation of sovereign states between 1858 and 1863, overthrown by a liberal civil war.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Pressure for federalism had grown in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-new-granada">Republic of New Granada</a>, and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-panama">Panama</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioquia-department">Antioquia</a> and other regions had become self-governing states. The constitution of 1858, under the conservative president <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mariano-ospina-rodriguez">Mariano Ospina Rodríguez</a>, created the Granadine Confederation, a union of eight states with a weak central government in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bogota">Bogotá</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The states had their own constitutions, armies and elections. Laws passed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mariano-ospina-rodriguez">Ospina</a>'s government to control state elections and armies were seen by liberals as an attack on state <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a>. In 1860 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tomas-cipriano-de-mosquera">Tomás Cipriano de Mosquera</a>, governor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/state-of-cauca">State of Cauca</a>, rebelled and declared Cauca separate from the confederation, starting a civil war.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tomas-cipriano-de-mosquera">Mosquera</a> captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bogota">Bogotá</a> in July 1861 and took power, expelling the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuits</a> and confiscating church lands. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rionegro-convention">Rionegro Convention</a> of 1863 replaced the confederation with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/united-states-of-colombia">United States of Colombia</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/granadine-confederation.jpg" alt="Granadine Confederation" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Fibonacci · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_New_Granada.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1858 CE – 1863 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Bogotá</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Mariano Ospina Rodríguez, Tomás Cipriano de Mosquera</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Roman Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Spanish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/colombia">Colombia</a>, <a href="/countries/panama">Panama</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Confederación Granadina</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1860&amp;focus=granadine-confederation" aria-label="Granadine Confederation on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2625 2005 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Granadine Confederation lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M2945 2261L2945 2261M2945 2261L2945 2261"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M2945 2261h0M2945 2261h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2945 2261h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M2945 2261h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Bogotá. <a href="/atlas?year=1860&amp;focus=granadine-confederation">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
